# Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): a fair coin chooses between diverging and
# tossing two fair coins (0 is heads) observed to show at least one head.  The probability that
# the last toss is heads is 2/7 under cwp (wp/wlp(1)), 6/7 under cwlp and 2/3 under r2.
# Expected: valid (cwp is 2/7 <= 0.3).  The reduction asks wp_q(S, [y = 0]) <= q for q = 0.3,
# a blocked run being worth q and a diverging one 0: 1/2 * (1/2 + q/4) = 1/4 + q/8 = 0.2875,
# and 1/4 + q/8 <= q exactly when q >= 2/7.  The reduction notes on stderr that the bound is
# checked at the feasible initial states (the program has a loop).
nat x;
nat y;
{
	while (true) {
		skip;
	}
}[1/2]{
	{
		x := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		x := 1;
	}
	{
		y := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		y := 1;
	}
	observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
}
?Ex [[y = 0]] <= 0.3
